/**
  @page ci-index Continuous integration
  @brief Inspect branch commits, workflow outcomes and generated reports.

  The tables below collect the latest workflow runs for `master` and `develop`.
  Each branch heading identifies its current commit; each workflow row links
  to the commit actually checked by that run.

  @section ci-status Current status

  The **Workflow run** link opens the execution and job logs. **Report** opens the
  generated summary when a matching report is available for that commit and
  run attempt.

  @section ci-reading Interpret a result

  A passing result applies to the commit shown in its row. An **older commit**
  label identifies a run that predates the current branch head. The Labeler
  row records pull-request labeling activity; it can therefore refer to a
  different commit from the branch's build and numerical tests.

  Running and queued states describe work in progress. For coverage, the
  Tests run's **Coverage / Finalize** job supplies the combined result after
  all required contributions and publication receipts have been checked.
  The Benchmarks run contains the campaign validation, pooling and publication
  jobs. Their outcomes establish whether the complete result set was published.

*/
